+/// Chroma resolution. Matches `ChromaSubsampling` in `core/src/format.rs`,
+/// which is `snake_case`, so the wire names are `luma444`, `luma422` and
+/// `luma420`.
+///
+/// This is not a quality slider wearing a different hat. Luma resolution never
+/// changes, so sharpness is identical at all three; what changes is how finely
+/// colour is stored. 4:2:0 keeps a quarter of the colour samples and is the
+/// right default for a photograph; 4:2:2 is the middle; 4:4:4 is the only level
+/// that keeps colour detail on hard edges, which is what text on a coloured
+/// background is. The argument, with the measurements, is in
+/// `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
+enum ChromaSubsampling {
+  luma444,
+  luma422,
+  luma420;
+
+  String toJson() => name;
+
+  static ChromaSubsampling fromJson(String value) =>
+      ChromaSubsampling.values.byName(value);
+}
